      "description": "tmux status line: green session tab, numbered window tabs with magenta active fill, language toggle, blue clock.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-sb\"><span class=\"ds-sess\">[juan]</span><a class=\"ds-win on\" href=\"#\">0:perfil*</a><a class=\"ds-win\" href=\"#\">1:experiencia</a><a class=\"ds-win\" href=\"#\">2:proyectos</a><span class=\"ds-sp\"></span><button class=\"ds-lang on\">es</button><button class=\"ds-lang\">en</button><span class=\"ds-clock\">01:17</span></nav>",
      "css": ":host{--bg:#1e1e2e;--mantle:#181825;--surface:#313244;--fg:#cdd6f4;--muted:#a6adc8;--red:#f38ba8;--orange:#fab387;--yellow:#f9e2af;--green:#a6e3a1;--cyan:#94e2d5;--blue:#89b4fa;--magenta:#cba6f7;--ease-out:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)} .ds-sb{font-family:'JetBrains Mono',ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:13px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1ch;height:28px;line-height:28px;background:var(--mantle);border-bottom:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 20%,transparent)} .ds-sess{background:var(--green);color:var(--bg);font-weight:700;padding:0 1ch} .ds-win{padding:0 1ch;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;transition:color .2s,background-color .2s} .ds-win:hover{color:var(--fg)} .ds-win.on{background:var(--magenta);color:var(--bg);font-weight:700} .ds-win:focus-visible,.ds-lang:focus-visible{outline:2px dashed var(--yellow);outline-offset:3px} .ds-sp{flex:1} .ds-lang{font:inherit;background:none;border:0;cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted);padding:0 .5ch} .ds-lang:hover,.ds-lang.on{color:var(--fg)} .ds-lang.on{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px;text-decoration-color:var(--green)} .ds-clock{background:var(--blue);color:var(--bg);padding:0 1ch}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Shell Prompt with Caret",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "pane",
      "description": "Typed command line with the blinking full-height block caret.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-prompt\"><span class=\"u\">juan</span><span class=\"m\">@</span><span class=\"h\">udc</span><span class=\"m\">:</span><span class=\"p\">~/proyectos</span><span class=\"m\">$ </span>ls<span class=\"ds-caret\"></span></div>",
      "css": ":host{--bg:#1e1e2e;--mantle:#181825;--surface:#313244;--fg:#cdd6f4;--muted:#a6adc8;--red:#f38ba8;--orange:#fab387;--yellow:#f9e2af;--green:#a6e3a1;--cyan:#94e2d5;--blue:#89b4fa;--magenta:#cba6f7;--ease-out:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)} .ds-prompt{font-family:'JetBrains Mono',ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:15px;line-height:24px;font-variant-ligatures:none;padding:8px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg)} .u{color:var(--green);font-weight:700} .h{color:var(--blue);font-weight:700} .p{color:var(--cyan)} .m{color:var(--muted)} .ds-caret{display:inline-block;width:.6em;height:1.15em;vertical-align:-.2em;background:var(--fg);animation:ds-blink 1s steps(1) infinite} @keyframes ds-blink{50%{opacity:0}} @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-caret{animation:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Night Walk in a Terminal",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Night Walk in a Terminal\"**\n\nThe whole page is a single terminal session drawn in characters. Behind everything, a fixed full-viewport canvas renders a living ASCII landscape (stars, aurora, moon, ridges, pines, grass, river, fireflies, campfire) that changes as the visitor scrolls from night to campfire. The cursor acts as wind and lantern in that field: characters scatter and glow around it, and a click sends a ripple through the landscape. Content sits on top in tmux-like panes framed with box-drawing characters, and text types itself in as each chapter enters view.\n\nThe system is a monospace grid. One face (JetBrains Mono) at one rhythm (24px line) carries everything, from the figlet ANSI Shadow display headings to the form fields. Colour comes from six well-known terminal palettes, and the active palette recolours every surface, including the canvas scene. The density is the density of a real terminal: generous line spacing, ch-unit gutters, no rounded corners, no card grid. The rejection is explicit. This is not the static green-on-black hacker page and not a grid of cards.\n\nPersonality never blocks scanning. Every pane is a real shell idiom (`neofetch`, `git log`, `ls`, `finger`, a mail prompt), so a recruiter reads facts in a form they already recognise.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One monospace face, one 24px line grid, sizes in ch and line multiples.",
      "Six swappable terminal palettes; every colour is a theme variable, nothing is fixed to one palette.",
      "Box-drawing frames (single `┌─┐` and double `╔═╗`) instead of borders and radii.",
      "A full-bleed canvas character landscape behind all content, reacting to cursor, click and scroll.",
      "Motion is terminal motion: typing, stepped print-in, blinking block caret, lolcat hue drift."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Palette-Is-a-Variable Rule",
        "body": "Every colour in the UI and in the canvas scene reads from the active theme's role variables. A new surface that hardcodes a hex will break on five of the six themes.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Seven-Accent Rule",
        "body": "Accents come only from the ANSI set (red, orange, yellow, green, cyan, blue, magenta). No tints, gradients or new hues; the lolcat rainbow on the name is the single exception and is generated per column in HSL.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Face Rule",
        "body": "JetBrains Mono is the only family. Hierarchy comes from figlet, weight (400/700/800) and colour, never from a second typeface.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Grid Line Rule",
        "body": "Vertical spacing is a multiple or half of the 24px line. Pane frames are computed in whole character cells against the same line, so anything that breaks the line rhythm breaks the frame.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Clear-the-Field Rule",
        "body": "Anything readable sits on mantle or on a cleared region of the canvas. Never place body text over live landscape characters.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** read every colour from the theme role variables so all six palettes, and the canvas scene, recolour together.",
      "**Do** keep spacing on the 24px line and in ch units; size new panes so the box-drawing frame lands on whole cells.",
      "**Do** express a new section as a real shell idiom inside a pane, opened by a typed prompt.",
      "**Do** give each chapter one ANSI accent and use it for its figlet heading and titles.",
      "**Do** honour reduced motion: typing completes instantly, print-in is skipped, the lolcat drift and the canvas wind stop.",
      "**Do** convert any new photo or screenshot to ASCII rather than showing the raster."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add a second typeface, rounded corners, or CSS borders where a box-drawing frame belongs.",
      "**Don't** put body text directly over live canvas characters; it goes on a pane or a cleared region with the base halo.",
      "**Don't** use red as the fill of a primary action.",
      "**Don't** build card grids; content belongs in panes that read as terminal output.",
      "**Don't** fall back to static green-on-black; the world is the full themed palette."
    ]
  }
}